# Define public Cell API contract

## Objective
Document and lock the Cell type's public API before implementation. Cell is the most fundamental type - changes here ripple everywhere.

## Cell Contract

### Layout (16 bytes, non-negotiable)
#[repr(C, align(16))]
pub struct Cell {
    pub content: CellContent,  // 4 bytes
    pub fg: PackedRgba,        // 4 bytes
    pub bg: PackedRgba,        // 4 bytes
    pub attrs: CellAttrs,      // 4 bytes
}

### Why 16 Bytes?
- 4 cells per 64-byte cache line (perfect fit)
- Single 128-bit SIMD comparison
- No heap allocation for 99% of cells
- 24 bytes wastes cache, 32 bytes doubles bandwidth

### CellContent (4 bytes)
Encoding: [31: type bit][30-0: data]
- Bit 31 == 0: char (Unicode scalar value)
- Bit 31 == 1: GraphemeId (pool slot + width)

pub struct CellContent(u32);
impl CellContent {
    const EMPTY: Self;
    fn from_char(c: char) -> Self;
    fn from_grapheme(id: GraphemeId) -> Self;
    fn is_grapheme(&self) -> bool;
    fn width(&self) -> usize;
}

### PackedRgba (4 bytes)
Layout: [R:8][G:8][B:8][A:8] native endian

pub struct PackedRgba(pub u32);
impl PackedRgba {
    const TRANSPARENT: Self;
    const BLACK: Self;
    const WHITE: Self;
    fn rgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8) -> Self;
    fn rgba(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8, a: u8) -> Self;
    fn r(&self) -> u8;
    fn g(&self) -> u8;
    fn b(&self) -> u8;
    fn a(&self) -> u8;
    fn over(self, dst: Self) -> Self;  // Porter-Duff
    fn with_opacity(self, opacity: f32) -> Self;
}

### CellAttrs (4 bytes)
Layout: [31-24: flags][23-0: link_id]

pub struct CellAttrs(u32);
impl CellAttrs {
    const NONE: Self;
    fn new(flags: StyleFlags, link_id: u32) -> Self;
    fn flags(&self) -> StyleFlags;
    fn link_id(&self) -> u32;
    fn with_flags(self, flags: StyleFlags) -> Self;
    fn with_link(self, link_id: u32) -> Self;
}

### Cell Methods
impl Cell {
    const CONTINUATION: Self;  // Placeholder for wide chars
    fn is_continuation(&self) -> bool;
    fn bits_eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool;
    fn width(&self) -> usize;
}

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] API documented in code comments
- [ ] Type layout verified with assert_eq!(size_of::<Cell>(), 16)
- [ ] All methods have doc comments explaining purpose
- [ ] No pub fields that could break invariants later

# Define Event types contract

## Objective
Document and lock the canonical Event types used throughout ftui.

## Event Enum
pub enum Event {
    Key(KeyEvent),
    Mouse(MouseEvent),
    Resize { width: u16, height: u16 },
    Paste(PasteEvent),
    Focus(bool),  // true = gained, false = lost
    Clipboard(ClipboardEvent),  // optional, feature-gated
}

## KeyEvent
pub struct KeyEvent {
    pub code: KeyCode,
    pub modifiers: Modifiers,
    pub kind: KeyEventKind,  // Press/Repeat/Release
}

impl KeyEvent {
    fn is_char(&self, c: char) -> bool;
}

## KeyCode
pub enum KeyCode {
    Char(char),
    Enter, Escape, Backspace, Tab, BackTab,
    Delete, Insert, Home, End,
    PageUp, PageDown,
    Up, Down, Left, Right,
    F(u8),
    Null,
}

## KeyEventKind
pub enum KeyEventKind {
    Press,    // Key pressed (default)
    Repeat,   // Key held (when available)
    Release,  // Key released (when available)
}

## Modifiers
bitflags! {
    pub struct Modifiers: u8 {
        const SHIFT = 0b0001;
        const ALT   = 0b0010;
        const CTRL  = 0b0100;
        const SUPER = 0b1000;
    }
}

## MouseEvent
pub struct MouseEvent {
    pub kind: MouseEventKind,
    pub x: u16,
    pub y: u16,
    pub modifiers: Modifiers,
}

## MouseEventKind
pub enum MouseEventKind {
    Down(MouseButton),
    Up(MouseButton),
    Drag(MouseButton),
    Moved,
    ScrollUp,
    ScrollDown,
}

## MouseButton
pub enum MouseButton {
    Left, Right, Middle,
}

## PasteEvent
pub struct PasteEvent {
    pub text: String,
    pub bracketed: bool,  // True if from bracketed paste mode
}

## ClipboardEvent (Optional)
pub struct ClipboardEvent {
    pub content: String,
    pub source: ClipboardSource,
}

pub enum ClipboardSource { Osc52, Unknown }

## Design Notes
- Events are Clone + PartialEq + Eq for use in tests
- Modifiers use bitflags for easy combination
- Mouse coordinates are 0-indexed (terminal is 1-indexed)
- KeyEventKind defaults to Press when not available

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All types documented
- [ ] Derive Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq where appropriate
- [ ] Event can be converted From Crossterm events

# Implement CellContent with char/grapheme encoding

## Objective
Implement the 4-byte CellContent type that efficiently encodes either a single char or a GraphemeId reference.

## Technical Design

### Encoding Scheme
Bit 31 (type discriminator):
- 0: Direct char (bits 0-30 contain Unicode scalar value)
- 1: GraphemeId reference (bits 0-23 = slot, bits 24-30 = width)

This allows:
- 99% of cells (ASCII/BMP) to be stored without heap
- Complex graphemes (emoji, ZWJ sequences) stored in pool

### Implementation
#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
#[repr(transparent)]
pub struct CellContent(u32);

impl CellContent {
    pub const EMPTY: Self = Self(0);

    #[inline]
    pub fn from_char(c: char) -> Self {
        Self(c as u32)
    }

    #[inline]
    pub fn from_grapheme(id: GraphemeId) -> Self {
        Self(0x8000_0000 | id.0)
    }

    #[inline]
    pub fn is_grapheme(&self) -> bool {
        self.0 & 0x8000_0000 != 0
    }

    #[inline]
    pub fn as_char(&self) -> Option<char> {
        if self.is_grapheme() {
            None
        } else {
            char::from_u32(self.0)
        }
    }

    #[inline]
    pub fn width(&self) -> usize {
        if self.is_grapheme() {
            ((self.0 >> 24) & 0x7F) as usize
        } else if self.0 == 0 {
            0
        } else {
            unicode_width::UnicodeWidthChar::width(
                char::from_u32(self.0).unwrap_or(' ')
            ).unwrap_or(1)
        }
    }
}

## GraphemeId Structure
#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
#[repr(transparent)]
pub struct GraphemeId(u32);

impl GraphemeId {
    #[inline]
    pub fn new(slot: u32, width: u8) -> Self {
        debug_assert!(slot < 0x00FF_FFFF);
        debug_assert!(width < 128);
        Self((slot & 0x00FF_FFFF) | ((width as u32) << 24))
    }

    #[inline]
    pub fn slot(&self) -> usize {
        (self.0 & 0x00FF_FFFF) as usize
    }

    #[inline]
    pub fn width(&self) -> usize {
        ((self.0 >> 24) & 0x7F) as usize
    }
}

## Tests Required
- [ ] from_char roundtrip for ASCII
- [ ] from_char roundtrip for BMP chars
- [ ] from_char roundtrip for supplementary planes
- [ ] from_grapheme encodes slot and width
- [ ] width() correct for narrow, wide, emoji
- [ ] EMPTY has width 0
- [ ] is_grapheme() discriminates correctly

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] size_of::<CellContent>() == 4
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] No unsafe code
- [ ] Inline hints on hot paths

# Implement PackedRgba with Porter-Duff blending

## Objective
Implement the 4-byte packed RGBA color type with efficient alpha compositing.

## Technical Design

### Layout
[R:8][G:8][B:8][A:8] in native endian as u32

### Why Packed?
- 4 bytes fits in Cell's 16-byte budget
- Fast equality comparison (single u32 compare)
- SIMD-friendly for bulk operations

### Porter-Duff 'Over' Compositing
Result = src + dst × (1 - src.alpha)

This is the standard way to composite translucent colors:
- Fully opaque src (alpha=255): result = src
- Fully transparent src (alpha=0): result = dst
- Partial: blend proportionally

### Implementation
#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]
#[repr(transparent)]
pub struct PackedRgba(pub u32);

impl PackedRgba {
    pub const TRANSPARENT: Self = Self(0);
    pub const BLACK: Self = Self::rgb(0, 0, 0);
    pub const WHITE: Self = Self::rgb(255, 255, 255);

    #[inline]
    pub const fn rgb(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8) -> Self {
        Self(((r as u32) << 24) | ((g as u32) << 16) 
             | ((b as u32) << 8) | 255)
    }

    #[inline]
    pub const fn rgba(r: u8, g: u8, b: u8, a: u8) -> Self {
        Self(((r as u32) << 24) | ((g as u32) << 16) 
             | ((b as u32) << 8) | (a as u32))
    }

    // Component accessors
    #[inline] pub fn r(&self) -> u8 { (self.0 >> 24) as u8 }
    #[inline] pub fn g(&self) -> u8 { (self.0 >> 16) as u8 }
    #[inline] pub fn b(&self) -> u8 { (self.0 >> 8) as u8 }
    #[inline] pub fn a(&self) -> u8 { self.0 as u8 }

    /// Porter-Duff 'over': src over dst
    #[inline]
    pub fn over(self, dst: Self) -> Self {
        let src_a = self.a() as u32;
        if src_a == 255 { return self; }
        if src_a == 0 { return dst; }

        let inv_a = 255 - src_a;
        let r = ((self.r() as u32 * 255) + (dst.r() as u32 * inv_a)) / 255;
        let g = ((self.g() as u32 * 255) + (dst.g() as u32 * inv_a)) / 255;
        let b = ((self.b() as u32 * 255) + (dst.b() as u32 * inv_a)) / 255;
        let a = src_a + ((dst.a() as u32 * inv_a) / 255);

        Self::rgba(r as u8, g as u8, b as u8, a as u8)
    }

    /// Apply uniform opacity [0.0, 1.0]
    #[inline]
    pub fn with_opacity(self, opacity: f32) -> Self {
        let a = ((self.a() as f32) * opacity.clamp(0.0, 1.0)) as u8;
        Self((self.0 & 0xFFFF_FF00) | (a as u32))
    }
}

