# Implement Buffer with scissor/opacity stacks

## Background & Strategic Importance
The Buffer is the central data structure of the rendering pipeline - the 2D grid of Cells that widgets render into and the Presenter reads from. It has the highest bottleneck score (367.5) in the dependency graph because 13+ downstream tasks depend on it.

**Why This Is Critical:**
- Every widget renders to a Buffer
- BufferDiff compares Buffers
- Presenter reads Buffers
- Frame wraps a Buffer
- All layout calculations target Buffer dimensions

---

## Technical Design

### Core Structure

```rust
use tracing::{debug, trace, instrument};

/// 2D grid of cells with scissor (clipping) and opacity stacks.
///
/// # Design Rationale
/// - Row-major layout for cache efficiency during diffing
/// - Scissor stack for nested clipping (widget boundaries)
/// - Opacity stack for transparency compositing
/// - Both stacks always have at least one element (invariant)
pub struct Buffer {
    width: u16,
    height: u16,
    cells: Vec<Cell>,
    /// Stack of clipping rectangles; writes outside current scissor are ignored
    scissor_stack: Vec<Rect>,
    /// Stack of opacity multipliers; applied to cell colors on write
    opacity_stack: Vec<f32>,
}
```

### Invariants (MUST be tested)

1. `cells.len() == width * height` (always, after construction)
2. `width` and `height` are immutable after creation
3. Scissor intersection monotonically decreases on push (can only shrink)
4. Opacity product stays in [0.0, 1.0] range
5. Both stacks always have at least one element (can't pop below base)
6. Wide character at x sets x+1 to CONTINUATION

### Constructor

```rust
impl Buffer {
    /// Create new buffer filled with default (empty) cells.
    ///
    /// # Panics
    /// Panics if width*height would overflow usize.
    pub fn new(width: u16, height: u16) -> Self {
        let size = (width as usize)
            .checked_mul(height as usize)
            .expect("Buffer size overflow");
        debug!(width, height, size, "Creating Buffer");

        Self {
            width,
            height,
            cells: vec![Cell::default(); size],
            scissor_stack: vec![Rect::new(0, 0, width, height)],
            opacity_stack: vec![1.0],
        }
    }

    /// Create from existing area (convenience for widget rendering).
    pub fn empty(area: Rect) -> Self {
        Self::new(area.width, area.height)
    }
}
```

### Cell Access

```rust
impl Buffer {
    // --- Dimensions ---

    #[inline]
    pub fn width(&self) -> u16 { self.width }

    #[inline]
    pub fn height(&self) -> u16 { self.height }

    #[inline]
    pub fn area(&self) -> Rect {
        Rect::new(0, 0, self.width, self.height)
    }

    // --- Index calculation ---

    #[inline]
    fn index(&self, x: u16, y: u16) -> usize {
        (y as usize) * (self.width as usize) + (x as usize)
    }

    // --- Safe access ---

    /// Get cell at (x, y) with bounds check.
    #[inline]
    pub fn get(&self, x: u16, y: u16) -> Option<&Cell> {
        if x < self.width && y < self.height {
            Some(&self.cells[self.index(x, y)])
        } else {
            None
        }
    }

    /// Get mutable cell at (x, y) with bounds check.
    #[inline]
    pub fn get_mut(&mut self, x: u16, y: u16) -> Option<&mut Cell> {
        if x < self.width && y < self.height {
            let idx = self.index(x, y);
            Some(&mut self.cells[idx])
        } else {
            None
        }
    }

    // --- Unchecked access (for hot paths like diffing) ---

    /// Get cell without bounds check. Caller must ensure x < width && y < height.
    #[inline]
    pub fn get_unchecked(&self, x: u16, y: u16) -> &Cell {
        debug_assert!(x < self.width && y < self.height);
        &self.cells[self.index(x, y)]
    }

    /// Raw cell slice for iteration.
    pub fn cells(&self) -> &[Cell] {
        &self.cells
    }
}
```

### Cell Mutation with Scissor/Opacity

```rust
impl Buffer {
    /// Set cell at (x, y), respecting scissor and opacity.
    ///
    /// - If (x, y) is outside current scissor, write is ignored
    /// - Opacity is multiplied into cell colors
    /// - Alpha compositing performed if bg is transparent
    /// - Wide chars (width 2) set CONTINUATION at x+1
    #[instrument(skip(self, cell), fields(x, y, in_scissor = self.in_scissor(x, y)))]
    pub fn set(&mut self, x: u16, y: u16, mut cell: Cell) {
        if !self.in_scissor(x, y) {
            trace!("Write outside scissor, ignored");
            return;
        }

        // Apply current opacity
        let opacity = self.current_opacity();
        if opacity < 1.0 {
            cell.fg = cell.fg.with_opacity(opacity);
            cell.bg = cell.bg.with_opacity(opacity);
        }

        // Alpha composite if background is transparent
        if cell.bg.a() < 255 {
            if let Some(existing) = self.get(x, y) {
                cell.bg = cell.bg.over(existing.bg);
            }
        }

        let idx = self.index(x, y);
        self.cells[idx] = cell;

        // Wide character: set continuation cell
        if cell.width() == 2 && x + 1 < self.width && self.in_scissor(x + 1, y) {
            self.cells[idx + 1] = Cell::CONTINUATION;
        }
    }

    /// Set string at position with style.
    ///
    /// Returns the x position after the last character written.
    pub fn set_string(&mut self, x: u16, y: u16, s: &str, style: Style) -> u16 {
        let mut pos_x = x;
        for grapheme in s.graphemes(true) {
            if pos_x >= self.width {
                break;
            }

            let width = unicode_width::UnicodeWidthStr::width(grapheme);
            if width == 0 {
                continue; // Skip zero-width chars
            }

            let cell = Cell::new(grapheme, style);
            self.set(pos_x, y, cell);
            pos_x += width as u16;
        }
        pos_x
    }

    /// Fill area with a cell.
    pub fn fill(&mut self, area: Rect, cell: Cell) {
        let clipped = area.intersection(&self.current_scissor());
        for y in clipped.y..clipped.y + clipped.height {
            for x in clipped.x..clipped.x + clipped.width {
                self.set(x, y, cell.clone());
            }
        }
    }

    /// Clear entire buffer to default cells.
    pub fn clear(&mut self) {
        self.cells.fill(Cell::default());
        debug!("Buffer cleared");
    }

    /// Clear a specific area to default cells.
    pub fn clear_area(&mut self, area: Rect) {
        self.fill(area, Cell::default());
    }
}
```

### Scissor Stack

```rust
impl Buffer {
    /// Push a new scissor rectangle (intersected with current).
    ///
    /// All subsequent writes are clipped to this intersection.
    /// Call `pop_scissor()` to restore previous scissor.
    pub fn push_scissor(&mut self, rect: Rect) {
        let current = self.current_scissor();
        let intersection = current.intersection(&rect);
        self.scissor_stack.push(intersection);
        trace!(
            ?current, ?rect, ?intersection,
            stack_depth = self.scissor_stack.len(),
            "Pushed scissor"
        );
    }

    /// Pop the top scissor rectangle.
    ///
    /// Base scissor (full buffer) cannot be popped.
    pub fn pop_scissor(&mut self) {
        if self.scissor_stack.len() > 1 {
            self.scissor_stack.pop();
            trace!(stack_depth = self.scissor_stack.len(), "Popped scissor");
        } else {
            debug!("Attempted to pop base scissor, ignored");
        }
    }

    /// Get current effective scissor rectangle.
    #[inline]
    pub fn current_scissor(&self) -> Rect {
        *self.scissor_stack.last().unwrap() // Invariant: always ≥1 element
    }

    /// Check if point is within current scissor.
    #[inline]
    fn in_scissor(&self, x: u16, y: u16) -> bool {
        self.current_scissor().contains(x, y)
    }

    /// RAII guard for scissor scope.
    pub fn scissor_scope(&mut self, rect: Rect) -> ScissorGuard<'_> {
        self.push_scissor(rect);
        ScissorGuard { buffer: self }
    }
}

/// RAII guard that pops scissor on drop.
pub struct ScissorGuard<'a> {
    buffer: &'a mut Buffer,
}

impl Drop for ScissorGuard<'_> {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        self.buffer.pop_scissor();
    }
}
```

### Opacity Stack

```rust
impl Buffer {
    /// Push opacity multiplier onto stack.
    ///
    /// Effective opacity = product of all stacked values.
    pub fn push_opacity(&mut self, opacity: f32) {
        let current = self.current_opacity();
        let clamped = opacity.clamp(0.0, 1.0);
        self.opacity_stack.push(current * clamped);
        trace!(
            current, new_opacity = clamped, effective = current * clamped,
            stack_depth = self.opacity_stack.len(),
            "Pushed opacity"
        );
    }

    /// Pop opacity value from stack.
    ///
    /// Base opacity (1.0) cannot be popped.
    pub fn pop_opacity(&mut self) {
        if self.opacity_stack.len() > 1 {
            self.opacity_stack.pop();
            trace!(stack_depth = self.opacity_stack.len(), "Popped opacity");
        }
    }

    /// Get current effective opacity (product of stack).
    #[inline]
    pub fn current_opacity(&self) -> f32 {
        *self.opacity_stack.last().unwrap() // Invariant: always ≥1 element
    }
}
```

