# Implement LinkRegistry for OSC 8 hyperlinks

## Objective
Implement URL storage and ID management for OSC 8 hyperlinks.

## Background: OSC 8 Hyperlinks
Modern terminals support clickable hyperlinks via OSC 8:
- Start link: ESC ] 8 ; ; URL ESC \\
- End link: ESC ] 8 ; ; ESC \\

Multiple cells can share the same link by using the same link ID. The registry deduplicates URLs and manages IDs.

## Technical Design

### Structure
pub struct LinkRegistry {
    links: Vec<Option<String>>,      // ID -> URL mapping
    lookup: HashMap<String, u32>,    // URL -> ID for dedup
    free_list: Vec<u32>,            // Reusable IDs
}

### Implementation
impl LinkRegistry {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            links: Vec::new(),
            lookup: HashMap::new(),
            free_list: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    /// Register a URL, returning existing ID if present
    pub fn register(&mut self, url: &str) -> u32 {
        // Check for existing
        if let Some(&id) = self.lookup.get(url) {
            return id;
        }

        // Allocate new ID
        let id = self.free_list.pop().unwrap_or_else(|| {
            let idx = self.links.len() as u32;
            self.links.push(None);
            idx
        });

        self.links[id as usize] = Some(url.to_string());
        self.lookup.insert(url.to_string(), id);
        id
    }

    /// Get URL for ID
    pub fn get(&self, id: u32) -> Option<&str> {
        self.links.get(id as usize)
            .and_then(|slot| slot.as_ref())
            .map(|s| s.as_str())
    }

    /// Unregister a link (for cleanup)
    pub fn unregister(&mut self, id: u32) {
        if let Some(Some(url)) = self.links.get(id as usize).cloned() {
            self.lookup.remove(&url);
            self.links[id as usize] = None;
            self.free_list.push(id);
        }
    }

    /// Check if ID is valid
    pub fn contains(&self, id: u32) -> bool {
        self.links.get(id as usize)
            .map(|slot| slot.is_some())
            .unwrap_or(false)
    }

    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {
        self.links.iter().filter(|l| l.is_some()).count()
    }
}

## Link Lifecycle in Rendering
1. When drawing a cell with a link:
   - Register URL with registry
   - Store link_id in CellAttrs

2. When presenting:
   - Check if link_id changed from tracked state
   - If changed, emit OSC 8 open/close sequences

3. After frame:
   - Links not used can be unregistered (optional GC)

## Tests Required
- [ ] register() returns same ID for same URL
- [ ] register() returns different IDs for different URLs
- [ ] get() retrieves correct URL
- [ ] unregister() frees slot
- [ ] Free list reuses IDs
- [ ] contains() correct for valid/invalid IDs

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] No unsafe code
- [ ] Deduplication works correctly

# Implement Presenter with state-tracked ANSI emission

## Objective
Implement the core ANSI emitter that transforms buffer diffs into terminal output with minimal bytes.

## Technical Design

### State Tracking
Track current terminal state to avoid redundant sequences:
- current_style: Option<CellStyle> (fg, bg, attrs)
- current_link: Option<u32> (link ID)
- cursor_x, cursor_y: u16 (cursor position)

### Structure
pub struct Presenter<W: Write> {
    writer: BufWriter<W>,    // 64KB buffer
    current_style: Option<CellStyle>,
    current_link: Option<u32>,
    cursor_x: u16,
    cursor_y: u16,
    capabilities: TerminalCapabilities,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
struct CellStyle {
    fg: PackedRgba,
    bg: PackedRgba,
    attrs: StyleFlags,
}

### Implementation

impl<W: Write> Presenter<W> {
    pub fn new(writer: W, capabilities: TerminalCapabilities) -> Self {
        Self {
            writer: BufWriter::with_capacity(64 * 1024, writer),
            current_style: None,
            current_link: None,
            cursor_x: 0,
            cursor_y: 0,
            capabilities,
        }
    }

    /// Present a frame using diff
    pub fn present(
        &mut self,
        buffer: &Buffer,
        diff: &BufferDiff,
        pool: &GraphemePool,
        links: &LinkRegistry,
    ) -> io::Result<()> {
        // Begin synchronized output
        if self.capabilities.sync_output {
            self.writer.write_all(b"\x1b[?2026h")?;
        }

        // Emit diff using run grouping
        self.emit_diff(buffer, diff, pool, links)?;

        // Reset style at end (clean state)
        self.writer.write_all(b"\x1b[0m")?;
        self.current_style = None;

        // Close any open link
        if self.current_link.is_some() {
            self.writer.write_all(b"\x1b]8;;\x1b\\")?;
            self.current_link = None;
        }

        // End synchronized output
        if self.capabilities.sync_output {
            self.writer.write_all(b"\x1b[?2026l")?;
        }

        self.writer.flush()
    }

    fn emit_diff(...) -> io::Result<()> {
        for run in diff.runs(buffer.width()) {
            // Single cursor move per run
            self.move_cursor_to(run.x0, run.y)?;

            // Emit cells (cursor advances naturally)
            for x in run.x0..=run.x1 {
                let cell = buffer.get_unchecked(x, run.y);
                self.emit_cell(cell, pool, links)?;
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    fn emit_cell(...) -> io::Result<()> {
        if cell.is_continuation() { return Ok(()); }

        self.emit_style_changes(cell)?;
        self.emit_link_changes(cell, links)?;
        self.emit_content(cell, pool)?;

        self.cursor_x += cell.width() as u16;
        Ok(())
    }

    fn emit_style_changes(&mut self, cell: &Cell) -> io::Result<()> {
        // v1: Reset+apply strategy (per ADR-002)
        // Emit SGR 0 then apply all attributes
        // Optimization: skip if style unchanged
    }

    fn emit_link_changes(&mut self, cell: &Cell, registry: &LinkRegistry) -> io::Result<()> {
        // Open/close OSC 8 links as needed
    }

    fn emit_content(&mut self, cell: &Cell, pool: &GraphemePool) -> io::Result<()> {
        // Emit char or grapheme from pool
    }

    fn move_cursor_to(&mut self, x: u16, y: u16) -> io::Result<()> {
        if self.cursor_x == x && self.cursor_y == y { return Ok(()); }
        write!(self.writer, "\x1b[{};{}H", y + 1, x + 1)?;
        self.cursor_x = x;
        self.cursor_y = y;
        Ok(())
    }
}

## ANSI Sequences Reference
- Cursor position: CSI row ; col H (1-indexed)
- SGR reset: CSI 0 m
- SGR attributes: CSI n ; n ; ... m
- True color fg: CSI 38 ; 2 ; r ; g ; b m
- True color bg: CSI 48 ; 2 ; r ; g ; b m
- OSC 8 open: OSC 8 ; ; url ST
- OSC 8 close: OSC 8 ; ; ST
- Sync begin: CSI ? 2026 h
- Sync end: CSI ? 2026 l

