# Implement GraphemeId encoding with slot+width packing

## Background
Plan Section 5.1 defines the specific encoding for GraphemeId - the reference to complex grapheme clusters in the GraphemePool. This encoding is critical for the 16-byte Cell constraint.

## Encoding Specification
```
GraphemeId: u32
Layout: [30-24: width (7 bits)][23-0: pool slot (24 bits)]
```

### Bit Layout
```
MSB                                      LSB
+-------+----------------------------------+
| Width | Pool Slot Index                  |
| 7 bits| 24 bits                          |
+-------+----------------------------------+
Bits: 30-24  23-0
```

### Capacity
- Pool slots: 16,777,216 (24 bits = 16M entries)
- Width range: 0-127 (7 bits, plenty for any display width)

## Implementation

```rust
/// Grapheme ID: reference to interned string in GraphemePool
/// Layout: [30-24: width (7 bits)][23-0: pool slot (24 bits)]
/// 
/// # Design Rationale
/// - 24 bits for slot allows 16M unique graphemes (far exceeding practical usage)
/// - 7 bits for width allows display widths 0-127 (most graphemes are 1-2)
/// - Embedded width avoids pool lookup for width queries
/// - Total 31 bits leaves bit 31 for CellContent type discrimination
#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
#[repr(transparent)]
pub struct GraphemeId(u32);

impl GraphemeId {
    /// Maximum slot index (24 bits)
    pub const MAX_SLOT: u32 = 0x00FF_FFFF;

    /// Maximum width (7 bits)
    pub const MAX_WIDTH: u8 = 127;

    /// Create from slot index and display width
    /// 
    /// # Panics
    /// Panics in debug mode if slot > MAX_SLOT or width > MAX_WIDTH
    #[inline]
    pub fn new(slot: u32, width: u8) -> Self {
        debug_assert!(slot <= Self::MAX_SLOT, "slot overflow: {}", slot);
        debug_assert!(width <= Self::MAX_WIDTH, "width overflow: {}", width);
        Self((slot & Self::MAX_SLOT) | ((width as u32) << 24))
    }

    /// Extract pool slot index (0-16M)
    #[inline]
    pub fn slot(&self) -> usize {
        (self.0 & Self::MAX_SLOT) as usize
    }

    /// Extract display width (0-127)
    #[inline]
    pub fn width(&self) -> usize {
        ((self.0 >> 24) & 0x7F) as usize
    }

    /// Raw u32 value for storage in CellContent
    #[inline]
    pub fn raw(&self) -> u32 {
        self.0
    }

    /// Reconstruct from raw u32
    #[inline]
    pub fn from_raw(raw: u32) -> Self {
        Self(raw)
    }
}

impl std::fmt::Debug for GraphemeId {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {
        f.debug_struct("GraphemeId")
            .field("slot", &self.slot())
            .field("width", &self.width())
            .finish()
    }
}
```

## Integration with CellContent

CellContent uses bit 31 to discriminate between char and GraphemeId:
- Bit 31 == 0: char (Unicode scalar value in bits 0-30)
- Bit 31 == 1: GraphemeId (slot + width in bits 0-30)

```rust
impl CellContent {
    pub fn from_grapheme(id: GraphemeId) -> Self {
        // Set bit 31 to indicate grapheme
        Self(0x8000_0000 | id.raw())
    }

    pub fn grapheme_id(&self) -> Option<GraphemeId> {
        if self.is_grapheme() {
            Some(GraphemeId::from_raw(self.0 & !0x8000_0000))
        } else {
            None
        }
    }
}
```

## Tests Required

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_grapheme_id_encoding() {
        // Test basic encoding
        let id = GraphemeId::new(12345, 2);
        assert_eq!(id.slot(), 12345);
        assert_eq!(id.width(), 2);

        // Test max values
        let id_max = GraphemeId::new(GraphemeId::MAX_SLOT, GraphemeId::MAX_WIDTH);
        assert_eq!(id_max.slot(), 0x00FF_FFFF);
        assert_eq!(id_max.width(), 127);

        // Test zero values
        let id_zero = GraphemeId::new(0, 0);
        assert_eq!(id_zero.slot(), 0);
        assert_eq!(id_zero.width(), 0);
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_grapheme_id_roundtrip() {
        for slot in [0, 1, 100, 10000, 0x00FF_FFFF] {
            for width in [0, 1, 2, 4, 127] {
                let id = GraphemeId::new(slot, width);
                assert_eq!(id.slot() as u32, slot);
                assert_eq!(id.width() as u8, width);
            }
        }
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_cellcontent_grapheme_integration() {
        let id = GraphemeId::new(42, 2);
        let content = CellContent::from_grapheme(id);

        assert!(content.is_grapheme());
        assert_eq!(content.grapheme_id(), Some(id));
        assert_eq!(content.width(), 2);
    }

    #[test]
    #[should_panic(expected = "slot overflow")]
    #[cfg(debug_assertions)]
    fn test_grapheme_id_slot_overflow_debug() {
        let _ = GraphemeId::new(0x0100_0000, 1); // 25 bits
    }

    #[test]
    #[should_panic(expected = "width overflow")]
    #[cfg(debug_assertions)]
    fn test_grapheme_id_width_overflow_debug() {
        let _ = GraphemeId::new(1, 128);
    }
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] GraphemeId fits in u32 with documented layout
- [ ] slot() and width() extract correctly
- [ ] Integration with CellContent works
- [ ] Debug assertions catch overflows
- [ ] Tests cover edge cases

## Dependencies
- Blocks: bd-10i.3.1 (CellContent)
- Blocks: bd-10i.3.5 (GraphemePool)

# Create virtualization performance tests

## Background
Part of Progressive Rendering (bd-3t87). Performance tests ensure virtualization achieves O(visible) not O(total) complexity.

## Performance Benchmarks

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod benchmarks {
    use criterion::{black_box, criterion_group, criterion_main, Criterion};

    fn bench_render_100k_items(c: &mut Criterion) {
        let mut group = c.benchmark_group("virtualized_list");

        // Generate 100K log lines
        let items: Vec<LogLine> = (0..100_000)
            .map(|i| LogLine::new(format!("Log line {}", i)))
            .collect();

        let virtualized = Virtualized::new(items);
        let list = VirtualizedList::new(virtualized);
        let mut buf = Buffer::empty(Rect::new(0, 0, 80, 24));
        let budget = RenderBudget::unlimited();

        group.bench_function("render_visible_only", |b| {
            b.iter(|| {
                list.render(Rect::new(0, 0, 80, 24), &mut buf, &budget);
                black_box(&buf);
            });
        });

        group.finish();
    }

    fn bench_scroll_100k_items(c: &mut Criterion) {
        let mut group = c.benchmark_group("scroll");

        let items: Vec<LogLine> = (0..100_000)
            .map(|i| LogLine::new(format!("Log line {}", i)))
            .collect();

        let mut virtualized = Virtualized::new(items);

        group.bench_function("scroll_one_line", |b| {
            b.iter(|| {
                virtualized.scroll(1);
                black_box(virtualized.scroll_offset);
            });
        });

        group.bench_function("scroll_page", |b| {
            b.iter(|| {
                virtualized.page_down();
                black_box(virtualized.scroll_offset);
            });
        });

        group.finish();
    }

    fn bench_append_with_ring(c: &mut Criterion) {
        let mut group = c.benchmark_group("log_ring");

        let mut ring = LogRing::new(10_000);

        group.bench_function("append_single", |b| {
            b.iter(|| {
                ring.push(LogLine::new("New log line"));
            });
        });

        group.bench_function("append_batch_100", |b| {
            b.iter(|| {
                for i in 0..100 {
                    ring.push(LogLine::new(format!("Batch line {}", i)));
                }
            });
        });

        group.finish();
    }

    criterion_group!(
        benches,
        bench_render_100k_items,
        bench_scroll_100k_items,
        bench_append_with_ring,
    );
    criterion_main!(benches);
}
```

## Performance Requirements

| Operation | Target | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| Render 100K items | < 20ms | Only visible items rendered |
| Scroll 1 line | < 1μs | O(1) offset update |
| Page scroll | < 1μs | O(1) offset update |
| Append single | < 100ns | Amortized O(1) |
| Memory (100K items) | < 50MB | With 10K ring capacity |

## Unit Tests

```rust
#[test]
fn render_time_scales_with_visible_not_total() {
    // 1K items
    let small = create_list(1_000);
    let start = Instant::now();
    small.render(Rect::new(0, 0, 80, 24), &mut buf, &budget);
    let small_time = start.elapsed();

    // 100K items
    let large = create_list(100_000);
    let start = Instant::now();
    large.render(Rect::new(0, 0, 80, 24), &mut buf, &budget);
    let large_time = start.elapsed();

    // Large should be similar to small (both only render ~24 items)
    assert!(large_time < small_time * 2);
}

#[test]
fn memory_bounded_by_ring_capacity() {
    let mut ring = LogRing::new(1_000);

    // Add 100K items
    for i in 0..100_000 {
        ring.push(LogLine::new(format!("Line {}", i)));
    }

    // Only 1K in memory
    assert_eq!(ring.len(), 1_000);
    assert_eq!(ring.total_count(), 100_000);
}

#[test]
fn scrollbar_position_accurate() {
    let mut v = Virtualized::new((0..100).collect::<Vec<_>>());
    v.visible_count = 10;

    // At start
    v.scroll_offset = 0;
    assert_eq!(v.scrollbar_position(), 0.0);

    // At end
    v.scroll_offset = 90;
    assert_eq!(v.scrollbar_position(), 1.0);

    // At middle
    v.scroll_offset = 45;
    assert!((v.scrollbar_position() - 0.5).abs() < 0.1);
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All benchmarks meet targets
- [ ] Render time O(visible)
- [ ] Memory bounded by capacity
- [ ] Scroll operations O(1)
- [ ] No allocations during scroll

